  "answer": "This feature request has been made before: a scheduled shutdown/sleep timer (after N minutes or at a set time). PowerToys has no such tool yet. The earlier tickets were closed as duplicates of the main tracking issues (#28490, #17970), so you can follow and thumbs-up those. In the meantime, use the built-in shutdown command: press Win+R and run `shutdown /s /t X`, where X is the number of seconds (e.g. 1800 for 30 minutes). Run `shutdown /a` to cancel. You can also put this command in a shortcut (.lnk) or trigger it from Task Scheduler. Sleep is harder to do with a command line timer, and the tickets did not offer a built-in way to do it."
